[web/changes/organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005/05-feature-impact-review.md#FB44]
1:# Feature Impact Review - organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005
2:
3:Decision: GO_WITH_CONDITIONS
4:
5:## Decision
6:
7:GO_WITH_CONDITIONS. The change is confined to one organizer table and one new
8:organizer endpoint, and it never moves money by itself: the worst case is a refund
9:*request* that still has to be settled by an admin through the pre-existing
10:`confirm-refund` route. The condition is that refund settlement and its audit trail
11:stay exactly as they are.
12:
13:## Source of truth
14:
15:- Refund policy: `calculateTournamentRefundQuote`
16:  (`src/modules/tournaments/utils/tournament-refund-policy.ts:40`). Amounts are never
17:  taken from the client or hand-computed.
18:- Refund request: `TournamentPaymentRepository.createPendingRefund`
19:  (`tournament-payment.repository.ts:199`), which compare-and-sets
20:  `payments.refund_status` NULL to `PENDING_REFUND` and refuses a second request.
21:- Refund settlement: `PaymentsRepository.confirmLegacyRefund`
22:  (`payments.repository.ts:702`), reachable only through
23:  `POST /payments/admin/payments/:id/confirm-refund`, `@Roles(ADMIN)`.
24:- Fee state: `tournament_participants.is_paid`. "Paid through the system" means a
25:  `payments` row exists with `status = 'COMPLETED'` and `purpose = 'REGISTRATION_FEE'`,
26:  which is exactly what `findCompletedParticipantPaymentInTx` looks up.
27:- Authorization: `TournamentAccessService.isManager`, the same check every other
28:  participant mutation uses.
29:
30:## Affected
31:
32:| Area | Change |
33:|---|---|
34:| Backend, `tournaments.controller.ts` | new `PATCH :id/participants/:participantId/fee-payment` |
35:| Backend, `tournament-participant-admin.service.ts` | new `setParticipantFeePaid`, audit + broadcast |
36:| Backend, `tournament-payment.repository.ts` | `setParticipantPaidInTx` (the transactional flag write) |
37:| Backend, new DTO | `UpdateParticipantFeePaymentDto { paid }` |
38:| Backend, two spec files | constructor arity only |
39:| Web, `RegistrationTab.tsx` | payment badge replaced by a checkbox plus a confirmation |
40:| Web, `features/tournaments/api.ts` | `setParticipantFeePaid` client |
41:| Web, `messages/vi.json`, `messages/en.json` | 11 keys each |
42:| Schema | none |
43:| Payments module | none |
44:
45:## Negative cases
46:
47:| Case | Behaviour |
48:|---|---|
49:| Caller does not manage the tournament | 403, no transaction opened |
50:| Participant belongs to another tournament | 404 |
51:| Flag already equals the requested value | no-op: no transaction, no audit row, no broadcast |
52:| Tick with no payment row | sets the flag only, creates no `payments` row |
53:| Untick with no payment row | clears the flag, no refund row, no money movement |
54:| Untick with a COMPLETED payment and `refund_status` NULL | policy quote, one `PENDING_REFUND` request, audit on both rows |
55:| Untick twice across a tick in between | second call skips the request instead of hitting the compare-and-set, so the flag is not rolled back |
56:| Payment already refunded or refund pending | flag still clears, `refundRequested` reports `false` |
57:| Concurrent unticks | the compare-and-set inside `createPendingRefund` keeps exactly one request; the loser throws inside the transaction, so nothing partially applies |
58:| Client double-click | the row's checkbox is disabled while its mutation is in flight |
59:
60:## Security
61:
62:- The endpoint can only ever *request* a refund. Moving money still requires the
63:  admin-only settlement route and a proof URL.
64:- Ownership re-checked server-side; the client never decides eligibility.
65:- The refund amount is computed server-side by the shared policy. There is no code
66:  path where a client-supplied number reaches `payment_refunds.amount`.
67:- Every write is audited inside the same transaction via `AuditService.logUpdate`.
68:- A repeat refund for the same payment is impossible at both the
69:  `refund_status` compare-and-set and the unique
70:  `financial_ledger_entries.idempotency_key`.
71:
72:## Conditions
73:
74:1. Do not relax the admin-only settlement route.
75:2. Re-run `validate-workflow.ps1 -Strict` after the two other in-progress worktrees
76:   in this workspace are committed, since they are unrelated.
77:
78:## Evidence
79:
80:- `npx jest src/modules/tournaments/services/tournament-participant-admin.service.spec.ts`
81:  → 13 passed. Includes 403, cross-tournament 404, idempotent no-op, mark-paid
82:  creates no payment row, refund requested through the policy quote, manual mark
83:  skipped, and a repeat-untick case that asserts no second refund is raised.
84:- `npx tsc --noEmit` on the backend: the error set is unchanged from `HEAD` for the
85:  three pre-existing spec files. A fourth spec,
86:  `tournament-import-legacy-contract.spec.ts`, errors only because of unrelated
87:  in-progress edits to `tournament-registration.repository.ts` in the same working
88:  tree.
89:- Browser, 1568x833, real `RegistrationTab` with a stubbed mutation: three
90:  participants render correct checkbox states; unticking a manual mark opens the
91:  neutral confirmation; unticking a system payment opens the danger confirmation
92:  with a red action; ticking applies immediately with no dialog.

