[web/changes/organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005/00-discovery-brief.md#096D]
1:# Discovery Brief - organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005
2:
3:## Question
4:
5:What already exists for a tournament organizer to record a manually collected
6:registration fee, and for refunding a fee the system captured?
7:
8:## Findings
9:
10:| # | Finding |
11:|---|---|
12:| F1 | No organizer route writes `is_paid`. `PATCH :id/participants/:participantId` takes only `status`. |
13:| F2 | The only normal writer is `transitionPayment`, on gateway completion. |
14:| F3 | `markParticipantPaid` exists but is used only for auto-reconciliation, and it writes the flag with **no audit row**. |
15:| F4 | Manual marks already happen today without a payment row, at import and at guest creation (`row.isPaid ?? true`). The flag has always been able to mean "not paid through us". |
16:| F5 | `TournamentParticipant.payment` is nullable, so `payment == null` is a reliable signal for "no system money". |
17:| F6 | Refunds are two-phase and admin-settled. There is no gateway reversal call anywhere; the money moves offline against a VietQR image. |
18:| F7 | `createPendingRefund` is the single request-side entry point and already refuses a second request. |
19:
20:## Options
21:
22:**A. Organizer endpoint that requests a refund.** Reuses the existing two-phase
23:design, keeps settlement admin-only. Chosen.
24:
25:**B. Let organizers settle refunds too.** Rejected: it removes the only separation
26:between "records a fee" and "returns money".
27:
28:**C. Make a manual mark create a `payments` row with a synthetic gateway.**
29:Rejected: it would make a manual mark indistinguishable from real money in the
30:ledger and the refund math.
31:
32:## Decision
33:
34:Option A. The organizer gains exactly the control the request describes and nothing
35:more.
36:
37:## Open items
38:
39:- `markParticipantPaid` still writes the flag without an audit row. The new endpoint
40:  does not use it for that reason and audits its own writes instead; the old method is
41:  left as it is for its reconciliation caller.
42:- A follow-up could add an optional note to a manual mark, but no column exists and
43:  inventing one was out of scope.

