7:| S3 | Paid through the system, `refund_status` NULL | checked | `PAYMENT` | danger on untick |
8:| S4 | Paid through the system, refund already pending or refunded | checked | `PAYMENT` | danger on untick, then cleared with no second refund |
9:| S5 | Request in flight | previous value, disabled | unchanged | confirm button shows the loading state |
10:| S6 | Backend rejects | previous value restored after refetch | unchanged | closes, toast shows the server message |
11:| S7 | Filter `UNPAID` active | only unpaid rows render, all unchecked | none | unaffected |
12:| S8 | Empty division | table empty state | none | none |
13:
14:The `unpaid` summary counter (`participants.filter(p => !p.isPaid).length`) is derived
15:from the same `isPaid` flag, so it moves with the checkbox with no extra wiring.
16:
17:Transitions exercised in a browser: S1 -> S2 (tick, no dialog), S2 -> S1 (neutral
18:dialog), S3 -> S4 (danger dialog). S5 and S6 are covered by the disabled attribute and
19:by the refetch-on-error path rather than by a screenshot.

