1:# Implementation Log - organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005
2:
3:## 2026-10-05
4:
5:### Backend
6:
7:| File | Change |
8:|---|---|
9:| `dto/update-participant-fee-payment.dto.ts` | new `UpdateParticipantFeePaymentDto { paid }` |
10:| `tournaments.controller.ts` | `PATCH :id/participants/:participantId/fee-payment`, guard stack copied from the sibling participant route |
11:| `tournaments.service.ts` | delegation plus the sibling `broadcastRegistrationChanged` |
12:| `services/tournament-participant-admin.service.ts` | `setParticipantFeePaid`, plus `AuditService`, `PG_CONNECTION` and `TournamentPaymentRepository` injected |
13:| `repositories/tournament-payment.repository.ts` | `setParticipantPaidInTx(tx, participantId, isPaid)` |
14:| `services/tournament-participant-admin.service.spec.ts` | nine cases, constructor updated |
15:| `tournaments-lite-pairing.spec.ts`, `utils/registration-lifecycle.spec.ts` | constructor arity only |
16:
17:### Web
18:
19:| File | Change |
20:|---|---|
21:| `features/tournaments/api.ts` | `setParticipantFeePaid` |
22:| `messages/vi.json`, `messages/en.json` | 11 keys each |
23:| `manage/components/RegistrationTab.tsx` | payment badge replaced by a checkbox; `hasSystemPayment`; `handleFeePaidChange`; a `ConfirmModal` that switches wording and variant on whether a system payment exists |
24:
25:### Deviations from the plan
26:
27:- `registeredAt` is `participant.registeredAt`, not `payment.createdAt`. The shared
28:  projection does not carry `createdAt`, every other caller passes the participant's
29:  value, and with a `KICKED` trigger the fee is waived so the timestamp cannot change
30:  the amount.
31:- `setParticipantPaidInTx` instead of the existing `markParticipantPaid`, because this
32:  endpoint needs both directions inside a caller-owned transaction.
33:
34:### Defects found during review, and fixed
35:
36:1. **Repeat untick would have thrown.** After a refund is raised, a
37:   tick / untick / tick / untick cycle reached the compare-and-set inside
38:   `createPendingRefund`, which throws and rolls the whole transaction back, leaving the
39:   checkbox stuck on. A payment that already carries a refund state now skips the
40:   request and the flag still clears.
41:2. **`refundRequested` was wrong.** It reported `completedPayment !== null`, so a
42:   skipped second refund would still have told the organizer a refund was raised. It
43:   now reports what the call actually did.
44:3. **Other rows looked enabled but were inert.** `handleFeePaidChange` guarded on
45:   `if (feePaymentBusyId) return;` while only the busy row's checkbox was disabled.
46:   Ticking row A and then clicking row B swallowed the click with no feedback. The guard
47:   is now scoped to the same participant.
48:4. **A paid mark could be fabricated on a finished tournament.** The endpoint originally
49:   had no tournament-status gate at all, so `paid: true` was accepted on an archived or
50:   completed tournament. Marking a fee paid now requires `REGISTRATION_OPEN` or
51:   `UPCOMING`. Clearing the mark stays ungated, because refunds are raised after the
52:   event has run.
53:
54:The first three were found by reading the code against the toggle cycle the UI allows.
55:The fourth was found by comparing this endpoint against its siblings. None of them failed
56:a test first, which is why a case was added for each afterwards.
57:
58:### Mutation check on the refund guard
59:
60:The repeat-untick test was verified to be able to fail. With the guard reverted to
61:`if (completedPayment)`, the suite goes to 12 passed / 1 failed. Restored, it passes. A
62:guard test that passes against unguarded code proves nothing, so this was run rather than
63:assumed.
64:
65:### Tournament-status gates: what was actually verified
66:
67:Measured, not assumed:
68:
69:| Method | File and line | Gate |
70:|---|---|---|
71:| `addTeamMember` | `tournament-registration.service.ts:769-774` | requires `REGISTRATION_OPEN` or `UPCOMING` |
72:| `withdraw` | `tournament-registration.service.ts:871-875` | rejects `IN_PROGRESS`, `COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED` |
73:| `kickParticipant` | `tournament-registration.service.ts:1091-1117` | none; authorization only |
74:| `updateParticipantStatus` | `tournament-participant-admin.service.ts:202-206` | requires `REGISTRATION_OPEN` |
75:| `setParticipantFeePaid` | this change | `paid` requires `REGISTRATION_OPEN` or `UPCOMING`; `paid: false` ungated |
76:
77:So there is no single house pattern to copy: the operations disagree with each other.
78:The split applied here is therefore a judgement, not a transcription:
79:
80:- **Tick** is gated, because it asserts money is in hand. Leaving it open let an
81:  organizer stamp "paid" onto any finished tournament.
82:- **Untick** is ungated, because refunding after the event is normal and legitimate. A
83:  gate here would break the case the feature exists for.
84:
85:This remains an **open decision for the user**: if they want unmarking restricted to the
86:registration window too, or ticking allowed on a completed tournament for late
87:collections, that is a one-line change with a matching test.
88:
89:### Known limitation, not fixed
90:
91:`findCompletedParticipantPaymentInTx` is `LIMIT 1`, newest first. If a participant ever
92:ends up with two completed payments that are both unrefunded, un-ticking raises a refund
93:for the newest only and the older one stays captured while `is_paid` goes false. This is a
94:pre-existing assumption of the whole refund design, shared by every existing caller of
95:that helper, so it is reported rather than silently changed.
96:
97:### Verification
98:
99:- Service spec: 15 passed. The refund-guard test was shown to fail when the guard is
100:  removed.
101:- Backend types: unchanged relative to `HEAD` for the three pre-existing spec files.
102:- Web types and lint: clean for the four files in this change.
103:- Browser: three checkbox states, both confirmations, and tick-without-dialog all
104:  observed; the throwaway harness was deleted.
105:
106:### Working tree note
107:
108:Both repositories also contain unrelated in-progress edits made by the user while this
109:work was running: `gender.helper.ts`, `tournament-registration.repository.ts`,
110:`QuickTournamentCreate.tsx`, the doubles registration flow, and a new
111:`quickTournamentFormats.ts`. None were touched or staged. The fourth backend type error,
112:in `tournament-import-legacy-contract.spec.ts`, comes from the user's
113:`tournament-registration.repository.ts` change, not from this one.

[web/changes/organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005/11-convergence-review.md#5CC1]
1:# Convergence Review - organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005
2:
3:## Requirements
4:
5:| # | Requested | Met | Evidence |
6:|---|---|---|---|
7:| R1 | Payment/status column becomes a checkbox | yes | `RegistrationTab.tsx` payment cell, observed in the browser |
8:| R2 | Can tick it yourself when the fee was collected | yes | tick applies immediately, no dialog |
9:| R3 | Untick a manual mark: no refund | yes | neutral confirmation, no payment row found server side, no refund row |
10:| R4 | Untick a system payment: refund | yes | one `PENDING_REFUND` request via the shared policy |
11:| R5 | Warning before it happens | yes | danger-styled confirmation naming the consequence |
12:| R6 | Do not ask, choose sensible defaults | yes | only one judgement call, the refund trigger, is recorded below |
13:
14:## The one judgement call
15:
16:The refund policy charges the platform fee on a withdrawal after three hours and waives
17:it when the organizer kicks someone. An organizer un-ticking a fee is a correction, not
18:a withdrawal, so `KICKED` was chosen and the full remaining amount comes back. It cannot
19:be milked: `refund_status` leaves null once per payment, and a manual mark never creates
20:a second payment row to refund. Recorded in `02-backend-feature-design.md`.
21:
22:## Completeness
23:
24:| Concern | Status |
25:|---|---|
26:| Dead prop or unreachable branch left behind | none |
27:| Ownership re-checked server-side | yes, `isManager`, plus a tournament-id match |
28:| Amount ever client-influenced | no, policy helper only |
29:| Refund settlement still admin-only | yes, untouched |
30:| Schema or migration | none |
31:| Dead code | the tray-style block layout pattern was not copied; the checkbox reuses the native input already used elsewhere in the app |
32:| Scaffold removal | the throwaway harness and its dev-server artifacts were deleted |
33:| Unrelated user edits | left untouched and unstaged in both repos |
34:
35:## Residuals accepted
36:
37:1. **A manual mark carries no note or receipt.** It is recorded in the audit log with
38:   the actor, but a deployment that wants a visible reason would need a new column.
39:   Out of scope, stated rather than half-built.
40:2. **No live request was exercised.** The local backend was not running and the
41:   endpoint is new, so the browser pass stubbed the mutation and the server behaviour
42:   rests on the service spec.
43:3. **`markParticipantPaid` still writes the flag without an audit row.** Pre-existing,
44:   used only by payment reconciliation; the new endpoint audits its own writes and does
45:   not use it.
46:
47:## Convergence
48:
49:Converged. No open blocker. Not pushed — a HighRisk money change is left staged for an
50:explicit go.

